Kevin Wayne <killedbyafoo@yahoo.com> writes:

> I recently compiled Nethack 3.4.3 for the first time. Now I'm trying
> to apply the Dump patch. I'm stuck with a Windows 98 box at the
..
> C:\Games\Nethack\Nethack-3.4.3>patch -p1 < dump-343.diff
> patching file 'dat/opthelp'
> Assertion failed: hunk, file patch.c, line 321
> 
> abnormal program termination

The assertion failure sounds like there is something wrong with the patch
utility you use. Maybe it is an old version?
Also, which version of the dump patch do you have? 
Does it say "Nethack 3.4.3 dump patch, version 1.2" on the first line, and
does it show 2004-04-27 as the date for the modified files?
(That is the newest one, but there is only little difference from version
1.1 for 3.4.3.)

> I verified that there is in fact a dat\opthelp file. There is not,
> however, a patch.c file. I counted 321 lines into the dump patch, and
> there didn't seem to be anything significant there. 

The patch.c is not part of nethack, it's the source of the patch utility
itself, and that's where the line number points.

> 1. What do I need to do to get the program to work? 

Try to find some other version of patch, preferably newer than the one you
used. 

> 2. Has the patch already done anything to my source code?

No. dat/opthelp is the first file to be patched by the dump patch, and
there is only one hunk in it to be patched. Since patch already crashed
there, it shouldn't have got anything done yet. You can verify this by
checking the timestamp of dat/opthelp.

> 3. Do I need to restore my source code to its previous state before I
> reapply the patch and/or try compiling again?

Not in this case. See above for the reason.

